{"id":"119-s-3012","label":"S. 3012","congress":119,"title":"Shutdown Fairness Act","latestVote":"2025-11-07","rollIds":["Senate:1:585","Senate:1:609"],"hasMetadata":true,"chambers":["Senate"],"congressUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/3012","metadataUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/s/BILLSTATUS-119s3012.xml","metadata":{"title":"Shutdown Fairness Act","introduced":"2025-10-15","latestAction":"Upon reconsideration, cloture on the motion to proceed to the measure not invoked in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 53 - 43. Record Vote Number: 609.","latestActionDate":"2025-11-07","policyArea":"Government Operations and Politics","subjects":["Appropriations","Congressional operations and organization","Government employee pay, benefits, personnel management","Military personnel and dependents","Public contracts and procurement"],"sponsors":["Sen. Johnson, Ron [R-WI]"],"cosponsors":["Sen. Budd, Ted [R-NC]","Sen. Cassidy, Bill [R-LA]","Sen. Crapo, Mike [R-ID]","Sen. Cotton, Tom [R-AR]","Sen. Risch, James E. [R-ID]","Sen. Sullivan, Dan [R-AK]","Sen. Young, Todd [R-IN]","Sen. Lee, Mike [R-UT]","Sen. Barrasso, John [R-WY]","Sen. Hoeven, John [R-ND]","Sen. McCormick, David [R-PA]","Sen. Scott, Rick [R-FL]","Sen. Lankford, James [R-OK]"],"committees":[],"laws":[],"committeeReports":[],"costEstimates":[],"relatedBills":[{"title":"Shutdown Fairness Act","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/3001"},{"title":"Shutdown Fairness Act","relationship":"Identical bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5801"},{"title":"Pay the People Act","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/3066"}],"textVersions":[{"date":"2025-10-16","stage":"Placed on Calendar Senate","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119s3012pcs/xml/BILLS-119s3012pcs.xml"}],"summaries":[{"date":"2025-10-15","stage":"Introduced in Senate","text":"Shutdown Fairness Act\n\nThis bill provides appropriations to pay federal employees who work during a government shutdown.\n\nSpecifically, the bill provides appropriations for federal agencies to provide standard rates of pay, allowances, pay differentials, benefits, and other payments to excepted employees for work performed during any period in which interim continuing appropriations or full-year appropriations are not in effect for a fiscal year (i.e., a government shutdown). An excepted employee is an employee who is required to work during a government shutdown.\n\nUnder current law, excepted employees are not paid until the government shutdown is over. This bill provides appropriations to pay excepted employees during a government shutdown. The bill also specifies that the term excepted employee includes certain contractors who support federal employees during a government shutdown and members of the Armed Forces who are on active duty. \n\nA federal agency may not use the funds provided by this bill during any period in which continuing appropriations are in effect for the purpose of paying excepted employees of the agency.\n\nThe bill must take effect as if it had been enacted on September 30, 2025."}],"actions":[{"date":"2025-11-07","text":"Upon reconsideration, cloture on the motion to proceed to the measure not invoked in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 53 - 43. Record Vote Number: 609."},{"date":"2025-11-07","text":"Motion by Senator Thune to reconsider the vote by which cloture on the motion to proceed to S. 3012 was not invoked (Record Vote No. 585) agreed to in Senate by Voice Vote. (CR S7996)"},{"date":"2025-11-07","text":"Motion to proceed to consideration of the motion to reconsider the vote by which cloture on the motion to proceed to S. 3012 was not invoked (Record Vote No. 585) agreed to in Senate by Voice Vote. (CR S7996)"},{"date":"2025-10-23","text":"Motion by Senator Thune to reconsider the vote by which cloture on the motion to proceed to S.